---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import PlanningCTA from '../components/PlanningCTA.astro';
import { images } from '../data/assets';
const breadcrumbs=[{label:'Where We Serve',href:'/where-we-serve/'}];
---
<BaseLayout title="U.S.-Based Group Travel Planning for Worldwide Trips | Talon Expeditions" description="Talon Expeditions is a U.S.-based group travel planning company serving clubs, communities, businesses, and private groups across the United States for trips to destinations worldwide." image={images.heroAlt} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}>
  <section class="page-hero" style={`background-image:url('${images.heroAlt}')`}><div class="shell"><Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs}/><p class="eyebrow">Where we serve</p><h1 class="section-title">U.S.-based planning. Groups from across the country. Destinations worldwide.</h1><p>Talon Expeditions is a U.S.-based group travel company serving travelers and organizers across the country, with trips planned to destinations worldwide. Planning can begin remotely from wherever the group is based, while destination-specific services are coordinated with the suppliers and specialists appropriate to the itinerary.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell definition-grid"><div class="definition-sticky"><p class="eyebrow">Service area</p><h2>National source market, global delivery.</h2></div><div class="definition-body"><div class="answer-panel"><h2>Where does Talon Expeditions plan trips?</h2><p>Talon Expeditions works primarily with U.S.-based organizers and travelers and plans travel to destinations worldwide. Groups can be concentrated in one city or have travelers arriving from different states or countries. The trip is structured around the actual departure pattern rather than a fixed local service area.</p></div><p>Our U.S. business correspondence is based in Miami Beach, Florida. That address establishes the company’s U.S. presence, but the service itself is not limited to South Florida. Planning conversations, group coordination, and traveler preparation can happen remotely, while destination operations rely on appropriate local suppliers, guides, instructors, or hosts.</p><p>For groups with travelers in multiple cities, one of the first planning decisions is whether to coordinate air centrally or define a common arrival point. The right model depends on the destination, flight network, transfer requirements, group size, and how much flexibility travelers need.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section soft-section"><div class="shell"><div class="specialty-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Common source-market patterns</p><h2 class="section-title">The group does not have to begin in one airport.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">We build arrival and departure logic around where the travelers are actually coming from.</p></div><div class="donor-grid"><div class="donor-card"><span class="card-index">01</span><h3>One-city group</h3><p>Useful for clubs, studios, schools, or communities whose travelers can depart together or reach one airport easily.</p></div><div class="donor-card"><span class="card-index">02</span><h3>Multi-city U.S. group</h3><p>Travelers may book from different origin cities and meet at a gateway or at the destination, with transfers built around a common window.</p></div><div class="donor-card"><span class="card-index">03</span><h3>Internationally distributed group</h3><p>For global communities or businesses, the trip can use a destination meeting point and a more structured arrival plan.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section dark-section"><div class="shell split-copy-image"><div><p class="eyebrow">Destination operations</p><h2 class="section-title">Worldwide does not mean generic.</h2><p style="color:#aaa">Every destination has different seasonal, supplier, transport, permit, guide, insurance, and activity realities. A global planning model only works if those local differences are treated seriously.</p><p style="color:#aaa">That is why destination pages and trip pages are added when there is enough real information to support them, rather than mass-producing thin pages for search engines.</p></div><div class="split-image" style={`background-image:url('${images.marrakech}')`}></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="specialty-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">U.S. correspondence</p><h2 class="section-title">One stable public entity layer.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">Travel support can be global while the company information stays consistent and easy to verify.</p></div><div class="office-grid"><div class="office-card"><h3>Talon Global LLC dba Talon Expeditions</h3><p>407 Lincoln Rd, Suite 6H166<br/>Miami Beach, FL 33139<br/>United States</p></div><div class="office-card"><h3>Phone</h3><p><a href="tel:+13057096099">+1 305 709 6099</a><br/>Use the contact form for detailed trip inquiries so the planning context is not lost.</p></div><div class="office-card"><h3>Email</h3><p><a href="mailto:sales@talonexpeditions.com">sales@talonexpeditions.com</a><br/>Group, supplier, media, and general travel inquiries can begin here.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <PlanningCTA title="Your travelers can start in different places. The trip still needs one coherent plan." />
</BaseLayout>
